{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794546895031,"sessionID":"ses_e2cad0affffeL00HGhtsGip9s0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d354850d0017tYWqe50pNk3UE","sessionID":"ses_e2cad0affffeL00HGhtsGip9s0","messageID":"msg_1d35458d0001jvO2taZer3QJfy","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a107eee122ac90d9","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md, lines 1-76\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Shared: Session Readers\"\n3: description: \"The read-only session reader package: one exact-id reader per runtime, the shared failure envelope, the capability table and the projection to the HistoryEntry list.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"session readers\"\n6:   - \"read session history\"\n7:   - \"session reader capabilities\"\n8:   - \"exact session id reader\"\n9: version: 1.0.0.0\n10: ---\n11: \n12: # Shared: Session Readers\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n17: \n18: This package reads one runtime session by its exact id and returns it as the shared `HistoryEntry` list that the history lookup core takes. It never writes. A reader opens a store read-only, proves the file or row belongs to the requested session, and returns a failure code rather than a partial list.\n19: \n20: The six decision-capture sweeps keep their own inline readers and remain the writers. Nothing here changes a save-time path.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. CONTRACT\n25: \n26: - **Exact id only.** A caller names a runtime and one session id. No reader guesses the newest session or lists a store.\n27: - **Read-only.** Files are read and SQLite stores are opened with read-only flags. The side-effect suite checks that no read changes a store's bytes or modification time.\n28: - **One envelope.** `readSession` returns `{ ok: true, source, items }` or `{ ok: false, code }`. It never throws across the boundary and never returns a partial list.\n29: - **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n30: \n31: Failure codes:\n32: \n33: | Code | Meaning |\n34: |---|---|\n35: | `locator_unavailable` | The id is empty or unsafe, or the runtime has no locator to resolve |\n36: | `capability_gated` | No reader exists for the runtime, or its switch is off |\n37: | `session_not_found` | No store record matches the id |\n38: | `session_mismatch` | A record was found, but its recorded id or path does not match |\n39: | `session_ambiguous` | More than one record claims the id |\n40: | `store_unreadable` | The store could not be read or projected |\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 3. FILES\n45: \n46: | File | Role |\n47: |---|---|\n48: | `index.mjs` | The dispatcher: `readSession` (projected entries), `loadSession` (raw records), the `capabilities` table and the failure envelope |\n49: | `identity.mjs` | Shared guards: safe session ids, path containment and the recorded-id check |\n50: | `project.mjs` | Projection from neutral records to `HistoryEntry`, with tool-call pairing |\n51: | `claude.mjs` | Claude Code transcript reader |\n52: | `codex.mjs` | Codex session log reader |\n53: | `pi.mjs` | Pi session log reader, following the live branch |\n54: | `opencode.mjs` | OpenCode SQLite store reader, which proves the session's recorded directory when the caller names one |\n55: | `devin.mjs` | Devin `sessions.db` reader over the session's main message chain and, through each compaction's `summarized_from` link, the threads before it. A recorded folder at or below the named folder passes, because Devin's hooks receive the project root. Falls back to the transcript file for a store without the session's turns |\n56: | `dsh.mjs` | DSH session log reader |\n57: | `cursor.mjs` | Cursor gate, which returns before touching any file |\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: ## 4. VALIDATION\n62: \n63: From the repository root:\n64: \n65: ```bash\n66: node --test .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/\n67: ```\n68: \n69: The matrix suite covers each runtime by store state, and the schema check validates projected entries against the history core's published JSON Schema.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 5. RELATED\n74: \n75: - [`../README.md`](../README.md): the shared hook helpers this package sits beside.\n76: - [`../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md`](../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md): the lookup core and CLI that consume these readers.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md, lines 1-76\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Shared: Session Readers\"\n3: description: \"The read-only session reader package: one exact-id reader per runtime, the shared failure envelope, the capability table and the projection to the HistoryEntry list.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"session readers\"\n6:   - \"read session history\"\n7:   - \"session reader capabilities\"\n8:   - \"exact session id reader\"\n9: version: 1.0.0.0\n10: ---\n11: \n12: # Shared: Session Readers\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n17: \n18: This package reads one runtime session by its exact id and returns it as the shared `HistoryEntry` list that the history lookup core takes. It never writes. A reader opens a store read-only, proves the file or row belongs to the requested session, and returns a failure code rather than a partial list.\n19: \n20: The six decision-capture sweeps keep their own inline readers and remain the writers. Nothing here changes a save-time path.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. CONTRACT\n25: \n26: - **Exact id only.** A caller names a runtime and one session id. No reader guesses the newest session or lists a store.\n27: - **Read-only.** Files are read and SQLite stores are opened with read-only flags. The side-effect suite checks that no read changes a store's bytes or modification time.\n28: - **One envelope.** `readSession` returns `{ ok: true, source, items }` or `{ ok: false, code }`. It never throws across the boundary and never returns a partial list.\n29: - **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n30: \n31: Failure codes:\n32: \n33: | Code | Meaning |\n34: |---|---|\n35: | `locator_unavailable` | The id is empty or unsafe, or the runtime has no locator to resolve |\n36: | `capability_gated` | No reader exists for the runtime, or its switch is off |\n37: | `session_not_found` | No store record matches the id |\n38: | `session_mismatch` | A record was found, but its recorded id or path does not match |\n39: | `session_ambiguous` | More than one record claims the id |\n40: | `store_unreadable` | The store could not be read or projected |\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 3. FILES\n45: \n46: | File | Role |\n47: |---|---|\n48: | `index.mjs` | The dispatcher: `readSession` (projected entries), `loadSession` (raw records), the `capabilities` table and the failure envelope |\n49: | `identity.mjs` | Shared guards: safe session ids, path containment and the recorded-id check |\n50: | `project.mjs` | Projection from neutral records to `HistoryEntry`, with tool-call pairing |\n51: | `claude.mjs` | Claude Code transcript reader |\n52: | `codex.mjs` | Codex session log reader |\n53: | `pi.mjs` | Pi session log reader, following the live branch |\n54: | `opencode.mjs` | OpenCode SQLite store reader, which proves the session's recorded directory when the caller names one |\n55: | `devin.mjs` | Devin `sessions.db` reader over the session's main message chain and, through each compaction's `summarized_from` link, the threads before it. A recorded folder at or below the named folder passes, because Devin's hooks receive the project root. Falls back to the transcript file for a store without the session's turns |\n56: | `dsh.mjs` | DSH session log reader |\n57: | `cursor.mjs` | Cursor gate, which returns before touching any file |\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: ## 4. VALIDATION\n62: \n63: From the repository root:\n64: \n65: ```bash\n66: node --test .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/\n67: ```\n68: \n69: The matrix suite covers each runtime by store state, and the schema check validates projected entries against the history core's published JSON Schema.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 5. RELATED\n74: \n75: - [`../README.md`](../README.md): the shared hook helpers this package sits beside.\n76: - [`../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md`](../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md): the lookup core and CLI that consume these readers."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794546894093,"end":1794546895031}}}}
