{"type":"text","timestamp":1794547017910,"sessionID":"ses_e2cad0affffeL00HGhtsGip9s0","part":{"id":"prt_1d3564f8e002O0gLHgBnaTKVw1","sessionID":"ses_e2cad0affffeL00HGhtsGip9s0","messageID":"msg_1d3561a7a001LKhSaQJnS1DMCc","type":"text","text":"Plan: one edit to `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md`, placing the `injected` paragraph in §2 CONTRACT after the existing contract bullets, with one source line per runtime. Proof: `rg -c \"injected\"` on that file must print at least 2.\n\n","time":{"start":1794547011470,"end":1794547017910}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794547017936,"sessionID":"ses_e2cad0affffeL00HGhtsGip9s0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3566020002hY3GHV1x0mvQJJ","sessionID":"ses_e2cad0affffeL00HGhtsGip9s0","messageID":"msg_1d3561a7a001LKhSaQJnS1DMCc","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb0823ba5237d282","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md","oldString":"- **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n\nFailure codes:","newString":"- **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n\n`loadSession` returns the raw neutral records. Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries. `loadSession` passes `injected` through and `readSession` ignores it, so only a caller on the raw path sees what the harness added.\n\n- Claude's `injected` source is `hook_additional_context`, one entry per hook context attachment.\n- Pi's `injected` source is the entry's custom type, such as `session-start-context`, or `custom_message` when it carries none.\n- Devin's `injected` source is `system` for a harness node and `unflagged-user` for a user node the harness wrote. The transcript fallback uses the step's own source.\n- DSH's `injected` source is the event's source kind, such as `repo-guards`, or `unknown` when it names none.\n\nFailure codes:"},"output":"Edited .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md\n+++ .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md\n@@ -27,8 +27,15 @@\n - **Read-only.** Files are read and SQLite stores are opened with read-only flags. The side-effect suite checks that no read changes a store's bytes or modification time.\n - **One envelope.** `readSession` returns `{ ok: true, source, items }` or `{ ok: false, code }`. It never throws across the boundary and never returns a partial list.\n - **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n \n+`loadSession` returns the raw neutral records. Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries. `loadSession` passes `injected` through and `readSession` ignores it, so only a caller on the raw path sees what the harness added.\n+\n+- Claude's `injected` source is `hook_additional_context`, one entry per hook context attachment.\n+- Pi's `injected` source is the entry's custom type, such as `session-start-context`, or `custom_message` when it carries none.\n+- Devin's `injected` source is `system` for a harness node and `unflagged-user` for a user node the harness wrote. The transcript fallback uses the step's own source.\n+- DSH's `injected` source is the event's source kind, such as `repo-guards`, or `unknown` when it names none.\n+\n Failure codes:\n \n | Code | Meaning |\n |---|---|\n","status":"modified","additions":7,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md\", \"oldString\": \"- **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\\n\\nFailure codes:\", \"newString\": \"- **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\\n\\n`loadSession` returns the raw neutral records. Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries. `loadSession` passes `injected` through and `readSession` ignores it, so only a caller on the raw path sees what the harness added.\\n\\n- Claude's `injected` source is `hook_additional_context`, one entry per hook context attachment.\\n- Pi's `injected` source is the entry's custom type, such as `session-start-context`, or `custom_message` when it carries none.\\n- Devin's `injected` source is `system` for a harness node and `unflagged-user` for a user node the harness wrote. The transcript fallback uses the step's own source.\\n- DSH's `injected` source is the event's source kind, such as `repo-guards`, or `unknown` when it names none.\\n\\nFailure codes:\"}"},"time":{"start":1794547015712,"end":1794547017936}}}}
