{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794547023652,"sessionID":"ses_e2cad0affffeL00HGhtsGip9s0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3567e49001OIfCtCyHxOS12E","sessionID":"ses_e2cad0affffeL00HGhtsGip9s0","messageID":"msg_1d3566eef001M02cyC0idXzYJN","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1f69cd112427533","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md","offset":24,"limit":28},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md, lines 24-51\n24: ## 2. CONTRACT\n25: \n26: - **Exact id only.** A caller names a runtime and one session id. No reader guesses the newest session or lists a store.\n27: - **Read-only.** Files are read and SQLite stores are opened with read-only flags. The side-effect suite checks that no read changes a store's bytes or modification time.\n28: - **One envelope.** `readSession` returns `{ ok: true, source, items }` or `{ ok: false, code }`. It never throws across the boundary and never returns a partial list.\n29: - **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n30: \n31: `loadSession` returns the raw neutral records. Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries. `loadSession` passes `injected` through and `readSession` ignores it, so only a caller on the raw path sees what the harness added.\n32: \n33: - Claude's `injected` source is `hook_additional_context`, one entry per hook context attachment.\n34: - Pi's `injected` source is the entry's custom type, such as `session-start-context`, or `custom_message` when it carries none.\n35: - Devin's `injected` source is `system` for a harness node and `unflagged-user` for a user node the harness wrote. The transcript fallback uses the step's own source.\n36: - DSH's `injected` source is the event's source kind, such as `repo-guards`, or `unknown` when it names none.\n37: \n38: Failure codes:\n39: \n40: | Code | Meaning |\n41: |---|---|\n42: | `locator_unavailable` | The id is empty or unsafe, or the runtime has no locator to resolve |\n43: | `capability_gated` | No reader exists for the runtime, or its switch is off |\n44: | `session_not_found` | No store record matches the id |\n45: | `session_mismatch` | A record was found, but its recorded id or path does not match |\n46: | `session_ambiguous` | More than one record claims the id |\n47: | `store_unreadable` | The store could not be read or projected |\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 3. FILES\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 52]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md, lines 24-51\n24: ## 2. CONTRACT\n25: \n26: - **Exact id only.** A caller names a runtime and one session id. No reader guesses the newest session or lists a store.\n27: - **Read-only.** Files are read and SQLite stores are opened with read-only flags. The side-effect suite checks that no read changes a store's bytes or modification time.\n28: - **One envelope.** `readSession` returns `{ ok: true, source, items }` or `{ ok: false, code }`. It never throws across the boundary and never returns a partial list.\n29: - **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n30: \n31: `loadSession` returns the raw neutral records. Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries. `loadSession` passes `injected` through and `readSession` ignores it, so only a caller on the raw path sees what the harness added.\n32: \n33: - Claude's `injected` source is `hook_additional_context`, one entry per hook context attachment.\n34: - Pi's `injected` source is the entry's custom type, such as `session-start-context`, or `custom_message` when it carries none.\n35: - Devin's `injected` source is `system` for a harness node and `unflagged-user` for a user node the harness wrote. The transcript fallback uses the step's own source.\n36: - DSH's `injected` source is the event's source kind, such as `repo-guards`, or `unknown` when it names none.\n37: \n38: Failure codes:\n39: \n40: | Code | Meaning |\n41: |---|---|\n42: | `locator_unavailable` | The id is empty or unsafe, or the runtime has no locator to resolve |\n43: | `capability_gated` | No reader exists for the runtime, or its switch is off |\n44: | `session_not_found` | No store record matches the id |\n45: | `session_mismatch` | A record was found, but its recorded id or path does not match |\n46: | `session_ambiguous` | More than one record claims the id |\n47: | `store_unreadable` | The store could not be read or projected |\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 3. FILES\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 52]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md\", \"offset\": 24, \"limit\": 28}"},"time":{"start":1794547023433,"end":1794547023652}}}}
